      "content": "High-dose iron supplements are dangerous without a confirmed diagnosis, as they can cause severe gastrointestinal distress and even organ damage. You should first get a blood test from a doctor to measure your ferritin and serum iron levels before starting any regimen. Only under medical supervision should you be prescribed an appropriate daily dosage, which often starts much lower than people assume to allow the body to adjust safely. Attempting to self-prescribe high doses to \"fix this fast\" is risky and could worsen your fatigue while introducing new health complications.",
